      en: "The Lapidary Gallery in the Vatican houses an extensive collection of ancient inscriptions and stonework. It was founded in the 19th century by Pope Gregory XVI. The gallery displays inscriptions from the Roman imperial period, Christian epitaphs, and architectural fragments. The exhibits are arranged chronologically and thematically. The gallery is an important resource for the study of ancient writing culture.",
